                                                              HOMEPAGE                 
in this our website main index page will be there and our goal is to achive the following things  ~
1.  The static home page must contain three frames. 
                                   TOP/ MIDDLE/ LEFT

2. Top frame: Logo and the college name and links to Homepage, Login 
page, Registration page, Catalogue page and Cart page . 

3. Middle frame: where we can see our descriptions  

4. Lower frame:  here we will se the list of departments 

For example: When you click the link “CSE” the catalogue for CSE Books should be 
displayed in the Right frame. Right frame: The pages to the links in the left frame must be 
loaded here. Initially this page contains description of the web site. 
..................................................................................................................................
less design our first index/home page -> 

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Online Bookstore</title>

  <!-- ================= CSS (design yaha hai) ================= -->
  <style>
    /* Sabhi elements ki default spacing hata do */
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    body {
      height: 100vh;
    }

    /* Bada dabba: grid se 5 hisso me baanta hai */
    .container {
      display: grid;
      height: 100vh;
      grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr;      /* left 150px, baaki right */
      grid-template-rows: 70px 40px 1fr;     /* logo row, nav row, baaki content */
      grid-template-areas:
        "logo   title"
        "nav    nav"
        "left   right";
    }

    /* Upar left: Logo */
    .logo {
      grid-area: logo;
      background: #f9be8d;
      border: 1px solid #000;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    /* Upar right: Website ka naam */
    .title {
      grid-area: title;
      background: #f9be8d;
      border: 1px solid #000;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    /* Beech ki patti: Home, Login, Registration... */
    .nav {
      grid-area: nav;
      background: #fde4d6;
      border: 1px solid #000;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-around;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .nav a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #000;
    }

    /* Left side: CSE, ECE, EEE, CIVIL */
    .left {
      grid-area: left;
      border: 1px solid #000;
      padding: 10px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;   /* links upar se neeche */
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .left a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #000;
    }

    /* Right side: yaha pages khulte hain */
    .right {
      grid-area: right;
      border: 1px solid #000;
    }

    .right iframe {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      border: none;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<!-- ================= HTML (structure yaha hai) ================= -->
<body>

  <div class="container">

    <!-- 1. Logo -->
    <div class="logo">Logo</div>

    <!-- 2. Website ka naam -->
    <div class="title">Web Site Name</div>

    <!-- 3. Top links -->
    <div class="nav">
      <a href="home.html" target="content">Home</a>
      <a href="login.html" target="content">Login</a>
      <a href="registration.html" target="content">Registration</a>
      <a href="catalogue.html" target="content">Catalogue</a>
      <a href="cart.html" target="content">Cart</a>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Left menu -->
    <div class="left">
      <a href="cse.html" target="content">CSE</a>
      <a href="ece.html" target="content">ECE</a>
      <a href="eee.html" target="content">EEE</a>
      <a href="civil.html" target="content">CIVIL</a>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. Right frame: name="content" wahi hai jo target="content" me hai -->
    <div class="right">
      <iframe name="content" src="home.html"></iframe>
    </div>

  </div>

</body>
</html>